# Canonical skills are hashed byte-for-byte (the Phase 3.2 run records and the
# A/B treatment attach skills/code-discipline/SKILL.md by SHA-256), and
# scripts/install.py requires LF front matter. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise produce CRLF files that the installer
# rejects and whose hash differs (Phase 3.2 risk R13).
skills/**/SKILL.md text eol=lf
